WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.185
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.080
CECILE LEROUX: UKG
is a leading provider

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.470
of HR talent, workforce
management, and payroll

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.000
solutions.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.030
And our focus is
absolutely on people.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.910
In fact, our tagline, which
is much more than a tagline,

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.170
is that our purpose is people.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.650
So when we think about some
of the major challenges

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.310
that our organization faced
and just like our customers are

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.610
facing is that the reality
is that the rules of work

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.780
are being rewritten.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.810
And we wanted to be part of
rewriting those rules of work

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.890
rather than just reacting
to what's happening in--

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.250
with so much uncertainty.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.160
So again, this need to
be incredibly adaptive

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.810
led us to really wanting to
take this DevOps approach.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.930
How do we implement life-work
technology internally as well

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.530
as for our customers?

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.200
One of the things
that we recognized

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.800
is that we had to be
hyper, hyper aware

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.280
of whether or not individuals
were nearing burnout,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.120
for example.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.069
What is it that we
could do to understand

00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:07.430
the makeup and the
cohesion of teams

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:12.240
to ensure that we had
consistent output and throughput

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.910
without overtaxing individuals?

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.400
Whenever you see a
challenge-- or whenever

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.410
we, certainly, at
UKG sees a challenge,

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:25.050
we think about it in terms of
what is the person approach?

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.610
How is that impacting
people individually and as

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.080
a whole, or teams?

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:36.450
And so we see opportunities
to actually bring new products

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.210
to the market based on
what our experiences are.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.580
We took the approach
of really adopting

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.850
some Cloud-native
attributes and capability

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:48.420
that would actually
support kind of decoupling

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.778
our releases from the
development lifecycle

00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:52.320
so that we could
accelerate and bring

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.160
more value to our customers.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.000
We have a significant
amount of cloud storage.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.700
But the most important
benefit that we

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.430
found with our
deployment, in particular,

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.740
of using some of the
Cloud-native capabilities

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.440
that GCP offered us to
change our delivery,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.940
reduce downtime significantly,
and also add resilience

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.940
to our overall
delivery-- so being

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.620
able to do continuous
integration

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.480
and continuous delivery,
taking advantage

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.950
of some of the metrics that
came, as well as deploying.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.750
In one of our
platforms, we actually

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.470
have deployed the entire
suite of Google Analytics

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.940
and embedded those
directly in so

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.340
that we can see where
usage is happening.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.370
The Google team was
incredible in understanding

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.930
how important those three
principles were to our teams.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.580
So we were able to get
at-- in particular,

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.990
I want to call out the AI and
the machine learning team,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:49.950
because we got so much from our
collaboration with that team,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.600
as well as across the board,
the leadership, the partner

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.110
team, the partner
organization, in really shaping

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.960
how we could take advantage
of some of those capabilities.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.310
[MUSIC PLAYING]

